nodecode-bulkpublish is a rewrite of bulkpublish's bulkpublish/hermes-bulkpublish:

https://github.com/bulkpublish/hermes-bulkpublish
commit 530589907c6f791aacd35e1f708dbe8949e7e87f

MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 BulkPublish (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the original carries no code. It is an Agent Plugins
manifest (plugin.json), one MCP server entry (mcp.json) pointing at
BulkPublish's hosted server with the user's key as a bearer token, and
thirty-three prose skills teaching the server's workflow. This cell is the
same connection, written once in Common Lisp: an MCP client over streamable
HTTP (initialize, tools/list, tools/call, session id, SSE answers), the
catalog of the server's own tools behind two model-facing tools and three
eval verbs, a /bulkpublish command, and the part of the skills a reader needs
at the moment of posting distilled into the (help :bulkpublish) manual. The
plugin marked the server untrusted so its harness asked before every
write-capable call; that ask is kept as one argument, "confirm", for the
tools that publish, reply, delete, approve, retry, update, schedule, cancel or
run a bulk action, and it can be turned off in the section.

What was left out, and why: the skills' per-platform pages (character limits,
media sizes, post types, forty-odd worked examples) are summarized rather than
transcribed, because the server documents its own arguments and the manual
only needs to keep the model from publishing the wrong shape; the plural
versions of the skills (inbox, RSS, recurring posts, team approvals) are
reached through the same tools, so no separate surface was written for them;
and the plugin's own favicon and README prose are not carried over.
